{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaEscapesSingleCrossing","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaEscapesSingleCrossing","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectionTen","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.SingleCrossingAlwaysBinds"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaEscapesSingleCrossing.selected_bond_unbinds_of_ratio_gt_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaEscapesSingleCrossing.selected_bond_unbinds_of_ratio_gt_one","kind":"theorem","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaEscapesSingleCrossing.lean#L145-L153","doc":"**The reconciliation, on the selected bond.** Given only that the selected\ninterface bond `G³` moves the diproton trace upward — the one number step 3 measured —\nthe log law makes the diproton unbound, and the single-crossing obstruction does not\napply: its grading is trivial here (`t3_grading_vacuous_on_gammaGamma`) and its\nhypothesis fails (`obstruction_conclusion_false_of_ratio_gt_one`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaEscapesSingleCrossing.obstruction_conclusion_false_of_ratio_gt_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaEscapesSingleCrossing.obstruction_conclusion_false_of_ratio_gt_one","kind":"theorem","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaEscapesSingleCrossing.lean#L136-L143","doc":"**The obstruction's `μ < 1` hypothesis is essential, not decorative.** For a channel\nscalar above one, carried through a writhe-`0` (γγ) grading, the conclusion of\n`nonneg_writhe_cannot_unbind` is FALSE — so a bond whose trace ratio exceeds one is\ngenuinely outside that theorem's scope rather than an unproved case of it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaEscapesSingleCrossing.bound_iff_ratio_lt_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaEscapesSingleCrossing.bound_iff_ratio_lt_one","kind":"theorem","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaEscapesSingleCrossing.lean#L124-L134","doc":"The mirror statement: a ratio below one binds. This is the content\n`single_crossing_binds` supplies for a single crossing, stated on the ratio alone. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaEscapesSingleCrossing.unbound_iff_ratio_gt_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaEscapesSingleCrossing.unbound_iff_ratio_gt_one","kind":"theorem","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaEscapesSingleCrossing.lean#L111-L122","doc":"**The sign law**: with a positive scale `α` and a positive trace ratio `μ`, the\nbinding `B = −α·log μ` is negative (unbound) exactly when the bond moves the trace\n*upward*, `μ > 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaEscapesSingleCrossing.t3_grading_vacuous_on_gammaGamma","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaEscapesSingleCrossing.t3_grading_vacuous_on_gammaGamma","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaEscapesSingleCrossing.lean#L101-L107","doc":"**The `T₃` / writhe grading is VACUOUS on a γγ word**: it multiplies the channel\nscalar by exactly `1`, so it can neither bind harder nor unbind. This is why the\n`t3_grading_cannot_unbind_pp` obstruction has no purchase on a γγ-selected bond — not\nbecause the bond defeats it, but because the grading it argues about is trivial there. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaEscapesSingleCrossing.writhe_normalisation_eq_one_of_gammaGamma","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaEscapesSingleCrossing.writhe_normalisation_eq_one_of_gammaGamma","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaEscapesSingleCrossing.lean#L96-L99","doc":"**The writhe normalisation factor is exactly `1` on a γγ word**, for any base. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaEscapesSingleCrossing.writheExponent_eq_zero_of_gammaGamma","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaEscapesSingleCrossing.writheExponent_eq_zero_of_gammaGamma","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaEscapesSingleCrossing.lean#L89-L94","doc":"**Every γγ word has grading exponent `0`** — immediate from `writhe_eq_zero`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaEscapesSingleCrossing.writheExponent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaEscapesSingleCrossing.writheExponent","kind":"def","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaEscapesSingleCrossing.lean#L86-L87","doc":"The writhe grading exponent `e = writhe w / 2` of the `T₃` normalisation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaEscapesSingleCrossing.interfaceBond_three_length_ne_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaEscapesSingleCrossing.interfaceBond_three_length_ne_one","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaEscapesSingleCrossing.lean#L80-L82","doc":"The selected bond has six crossings, so a fortiori it is not one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaEscapesSingleCrossing.interfaceBond_ne_singleCrossing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaEscapesSingleCrossing.interfaceBond_ne_singleCrossing","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaEscapesSingleCrossing.lean#L74-L78","doc":"In particular no interface bond `G^m` is a single crossing: it has `2m` crossings\n(`interfaceBond_length`), which is never one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaEscapesSingleCrossing.gammaGamma_ne_singleCrossing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaEscapesSingleCrossing.gammaGamma_ne_singleCrossing","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaEscapesSingleCrossing.lean#L64-L72","doc":"**No non-empty γγ word is a single crossing**: γγ words have even length\n(`length_even`), and a single crossing has length one. ","signatureChunk":0}]}